    purpose: "Recover the same pending or already-consumed message batch without losing or logically duplicating delivery",
    settlement: "A stable run-and-boundary command receipt returns the identical batch after a crash between registry CAS and invocation recording; acknowledged messages do not reappear at later boundaries",
    steps: "restart restores native shared thread state -> Cognate replays recorded run steps -> consume command revalidates current recipient Team and Assignment -> matching receipt returns same ordered batch or new boundary commits next eligible batch -> agent continues at a safe model decision",
    variants: "stale Team membership, cancelled Assignment and private scope mismatch deny incorporation; retry cannot widen captured tools or mode; provider call is never interrupted"
}

// Team-level admission policy: a Team's authoritative limits bound how many of its own runs may
// overlap, independently of process capacity. Established by T2. The orthogonal process-capacity and
// workspace-disjointness policy is J-EXPERT-PARALLEL.
Instance j_team_admission of "CanonicalJourney" {
    actor: "User or OperatorAgent",
    capabilities: "team.converse, expert.converse, team.retry, team.handoff, execution.runtime.inspect",
    evidence_class: "observed",
    initiating_condition: "An active Team admits new Expert work while other runs of the same Team are unfinished",
    journey_id: "J-TEAM-ADMISSION",
    precondition: "The Team is active with an authoritative limits policy (maximum concurrent runs and admission batch); each admitted root resolves to a canonical workspace identity",
    purpose: "Bound how many of a Team's own runs may overlap from the Team's authoritative policy, independently of process capacity, and dispatch queued roots in the Team's configured batch",
    settlement: "Admission lane count derives only from authoritative Team metadata; a Team exceeding its maxConcurrentRuns waits even when process capacity is free; disjoint roots overlap only up to the policy; queued roots dispatch in the configured batch; client-supplied policy is refused before any effect; unknown or inactive Teams and invalid policy fail closed to full Team serialization; a recovered run may re-enter a different lane, which can only serialize more and never admits beyond the policy",
