    journey_id: "J-HARNESS-session",
    precondition: "The chosen CLI is installed on the server host; the Session's workspace lives in the local world; no run of the Session is active; SEA-Forge governance is off",
    purpose: "Run a turn through the CLI and fold what it reports into the same transcript, tool timeline and usage events the native agent produces, labelled with a truthful posture",
    settlement: "The binding is a durable explicit operator choice per Session, labelled harness-own-sandbox, harness-bridged-approvals or harness-uncontained; each turn runs the CLI process in the workspace folder with a minimal environment that carries no Workbench provider credentials; streamed text, tool calls (file edits with diffs when the CLI reports them), usage and the final message are recorded as the same domain events the native agent emits; the CLI's own session id is recorded so the next turn resumes it; a CLI failure ends the turn as a failed turn with a readable message; a binding to a remote, contained, SSH or WSL workspace is refused with the reason; binding is refused while a run is active; binding back to native is explicit and durable",
    steps: "operator binds the Session to a harness with a permission mode and optional model -> session.harness.bind validates the CLI, the world and idleness and records the binding -> the operator sends a turn to the harness agent -> the agent drives the CLI through recorded advance steps -> events fold into the transcript -> the CLI's session id is recorded",
    variants: "binding back to native; changing the permission mode or model between turns; a turn sent from the paired phone to a bound Session starts the harness agent, never the native one, a turn already in progress is refused on the phone with a readable reason rather than steered, and the phone may answer the CLI's permission request; a second turn resumes the CLI's own session; replay of a recorded turn reuses recorded outputs and never respawns the CLI; a server restart in the middle of a turn ends the turn as session-lost rather than repeating the CLI's effects. Guarantee gaps stated: per-tool authority checks, containment of the CLI's tool effects, protected-evidence blocking and settlement as agent.coding do not apply; evidence is what the CLI self-reports; cost is unknown unless the CLI reports tokens"
}

Instance j_harness_approval of "CanonicalJourney" {
    actor: "User",
    capabilities: "session.harness.bind",
    evidence_class: "proposed",
    initiating_condition: "A harness CLI asks permission for a tool call during a turn",
