    precondition: "The Session is bound to a harness that can route permission requests, in a mode other than full access",
    purpose: "Bridge the CLI's own permission requests into Workbench approvals so the operator allows or denies each one and the CLI resumes accordingly",
    settlement: "Each CLI permission request becomes a tool approval request on the run with the tool, arguments and permission class; the turn waits as a durable continuation; approving answers the CLI with allow and the tool proceeds, denying answers with a refusal and the tool fails with that reason; the decision is recorded as a tool approval decision; in plan mode state-changing requests are declined without asking; this is the CLI's gate bridged to the operator, not the Workbench's own approval gate",
    steps: "the CLI sends a permission request -> the adapter pauses the turn and returns the request -> the agent records the approval request and waits on a human-approval continuation -> the operator decides -> the agent answers the CLI through the adapter -> the CLI continues or reports the denial",
    variants: "a request the CLI withdraws is dropped; multiple pending requests are answered one by one; a structured question from the CLI is declined with a note to answer in chat; the full-access mode never asks and is labelled harness-uncontained"
}

